      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُ أَبَا جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ يَقُولُ: \"عِدَّةُ اَلْمُتْعَةِ خَمْسَةٌ وَ أَرْبَعُونَ يَوْماً\" كَأَنِّي أَنْظُرُ إِلَى أَبِي جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ يَعْقِدُ بِيَدِهِ خَمْسَةً وَ أَرْبَعِينَ يَوْماً \"فَإِذَا جَاءَ اَلْأَجَلُ كَانَتْ فُرْقَةً بِغَيْرِ طَلاَقٍ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4605 - Musa ibn Bakr narrated from Zurara, who said:\nI heard Abu Ja'far Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as) saying:\n\"The waiting period ('Iddah) for Mut'ah (temporary marriage) is forty-five days.\"\nImam (as) then demonstrated by holding up his hand and showing forty-five days.\n\"When the specified term ends, the separation occurs without the need for divorce.\""
        ]
      }
